 - `APP_SERVER_LOGS` - directory for adapter logs.
 
+### Proposed ChatGPT subscription route mode
+
+`--require-chatgpt-subscription` is an opt-in proposal for controlled ACP launches.
+Launch with a dedicated, clean, absolute `CODEX_HOME` and the pinned bundled Codex.
+The mode rejects ambient API keys, adapter provider/config overrides, and custom
+provider mutations. Native Codex starts with `forced_login_method=chatgpt`; fresh
+sessions require native `account/read` to report a ChatGPT account and use the
+built-in `openai` provider. Resume, load, fork, steering, and goal controls are
+unavailable in this first version, as are client-supplied MCP servers and
+additional directories. These unavailable methods are not advertised. The
+normal per-project trust overrides are not injected. Adapter file logging is
+disabled in this mode.
+An unauthenticated user must complete a separate ChatGPT login before creating
+a session. This check does not attest a paid plan, effective billing, or an
+immutable network route. The launcher must keep the profile and project config
+under its control throughout the session.
+
